  "id": "RLSA-2026:102714",
  "title": "Critical: ruby4.0 security, bug fix, and enhancement update",
  "issued": {
    "date": "2026-11-25 06:07:23"
  },
  "updated": {
    "date": "2026-11-27 06:10:28"
  },
  "severity": "Critical",
  "description": "Ruby is the interpreted scripting language for quick and easy object-oriented programming.  It has many features to process text files and to do system management tasks (as in Perl).  It is simple, straight-forward, and extensible.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* ruby: integer overflow issue in regular expression compiler (CVE-2026-93577)\n\n* ruby: integer overflow issue in CI/CD regular expression compiler (CVE-2026-97229)\n\n* ruby: integer overflow issue in regular expression compiler (CVE-2026-110264)\n\n* ruby: ruby: Heap-based buffer overflow via string case conversion (CVE-2026-132825)\n\nBug Fix(es) and Enhancement(s):\n\n* ruby4.0: Rebase to the latest Ruby 4.0 release [rhel-10] (JIRA:Rocky Linux-260673)\n\n* ruby4.0: Rebase to the latest Ruby 4.0 release [rhel-10.3.z] (JIRA:Rocky Linux-312591)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.",
